GPU vs CPU

CPU has 24 core inside a chip whereas GPU has 10,000 core inside the chip 
In CPU small calculation has faster speed rather than GPU
CPU is flexible and operate the operating system and applicationsbut GPU can't
GPU has 64 Bus width and 1.15 Terabytes/sec whereas CPU has 64 bus bit and gigabytes/sec.

If we need to evaluate buch of data then GPU is better rather than CPU.

There are 3 things in the GPU which do all the calcuation in it.
1. CUDA Core
2. Tensor Core 
3. Ray Tracing Core

1.Cuda is used to do binary calculation (add, sub, multi, divid) mostly used while gaming.
2.Tensor is used for matrix calculation (add, sub, multi, divid) mosly used in geometry transformation, Neura networks and AI.
3.Ray trasing is the largest but the fewest which are used in ray tracing algorithms.

In the Cuda core there is approx 4,10,000 transistors where 50,000 transistors performs the operation of A x B + C (called as Fused Multiply and Add).
It is the most of the work the gpu does. Other of the transistor does the Bit Shifting and Bit Masking and collecting the incoming operands and outputing the results.

Along this core there is 12 Graphic Memory Controller, 2 L2 Cache, PCIe Interface, NVLink, Gigthread Engine(Manages all the graphic clusters ).

SIM (Single Instruction Multiple Data) it is used to render the places in the game
